@h1 Syntax reference h1@

Every surface form Wit accepts, with its canonical shape, the AST node it
produces, and the rule that closes it. This is the "how do I write X" index.
For depth on any form, follow its guide link; for the exact node HTML, see the
@a |href /docs/reference/core-vocabulary/| core vocabulary a@.

@aside(class note)
Terms used below: @strong paramsSource strong@ is how a call's parameters were
written; @strong closeStyle strong@ is how it terminates. Both are recorded on
the AST and are observable with @@@code wit tour code@@@. See the
@a |href /docs/reference/glossary/| glossary a@.

aside@

@h2 Node call forms h2@

A call invokes a node. The parameter style you open with is the style that
closes the call — mixing them raises @@@code E_MIXED_PARAM_SOURCE code@@@.

@table |rows [[Form, paramsSource, closeStyle, Fixture], [Bare reference, none, bare, 04 bare-reference], [Named body block, none, named, 04 block-name-body], [Named body inline, none, named, 04 inline-name-body], [Dotted data access, none, bare, 04 dotted-access], [Parens, parens, parens, 05 single-named-param], [Pipes, pipes, named, 06 basic-named], [Record-arg, record, parens, 22 inline-single-field], [Form-fill body, form-fill, named, 23 template-invocation], [Colon-scatter, pipes, named, 24 body-scatter-single], [Flag param, pipes / parens, —, 06 flag-with-bang], [Opaque pass-through, parens, parens, 20 bare-node-passthrough], [Raw literal, none, named, literal-nodes], [Frozen literal, none, named, ast.ts frozen]]| |caption Call forms and the AST they produce| table@

@h3 Bare reference h3@

Resolves to a same-named definition. Binds nothing → an unresolved span.

@@@pre
@name
pre@@@

@h3 Named body — block and inline h3@

Opener and matching close on their own lines is a @strong block strong@ use
(body is @@@code Block[] code@@@). Mid-paragraph it is an @strong inline strong@
use (@@@code inline: true code@@@, body is @@@code Inline[] code@@@).

@@@pre
@blockquote
A quotation, set apart.
blockquote@

An @em inline em@ mark sits mid-sentence.
pre@@@

@h3 Dotted data access h3@

Binds a @strong data def strong@, not a node def. Numeric segments index a
collection. Unresolved → @@@code <span class="wit-unresolved">@a.b</span> code@@@.

@@@pre
@author.name
@sales.0.region
pre@@@

@h3 Parens h3@

Self-closing. Space-separated or colon keys. A multi-word colon value must be
quoted.

@@@pre
@img(src photo.jpg, alt A photo)
@h2(id intro, class lead) Title h2@
@x(k: "a b")
pre@@@

@h3 Pipes h3@

Each pipe is one parameter; duplicate keys are last-one-wins. Closed by
@@@code name@ code@@@.

@@@pre
@a |href /docs| |target _blank| Read the docs a@
pre@@@

@aside(class note)
Greedy-bind hazard: a pipes call with no @@@code name@ code@@@ on the same line
binds to the next matching close below it. Put pipes calls last, or close on
the same line. See @a |href /docs/reference/gotchas/| gotchas a@.

aside@

@h3 Record-arg h3@

An inline or multi-line record as the argument; self-closing. Hyphen
@strong or strong@ colon delimiter is accepted at a call site.

@@@pre
@card { title - Q3, status - shipped }
pre@@@

@h3 Form-fill body h3@

A bare opener followed by @@@code key: value code@@@ lines. Needs
@strong two or more strong@ content lines, or it is read as prose.

@@@pre
@contact
name: Ada Lovelace
role: Author
contact@
pre@@@

@h3 Colon-scatter h3@

A single-line body of @@@code k:v code@@@ tokens (no space after the colon).
Surfaces internally as @@@code paramsSource: pipes code@@@. A space after the
colon is prose.

@@@pre
@badge status:new priority:high badge@
pre@@@

@h3 Flag param h3@

A valueless parameter: a trailing bang in a pipe, or a bare flag in parens.

@@@pre
@task |title Ship| |urgent!| task@
pre@@@

@h3 Opaque pass-through h3@

The universal container. If @code type code@ names a core-vocab node it renders
as that element; otherwise it emits a @@@code <div> code@@@ carrying every named
param as @@@code data-* code@@@.

@@@pre
@node(type h2) A heading node@
@node(type box, role note) Body node@
pre@@@

@h3 Raw and frozen literals h3@

@@@code @@name … name@@ code@@@ makes the body one verbatim Text node
(@code raw code@); @@@code {{path}} code@@@ holes still expand.
@@@code @@@name … name@@@ code@@@ adds @code frozen code@ — even
@@@code {{…}} code@@@ passes through untouched.

@@@pre
@@style .lead { font-size: 1.2rem } style@@
pre@@@

@h2 Definition forms h2@

A definition declares a reusable node or a named value. Opens with a hash.

@table |rows [[Form, AST shape, Note, Fixture], [Single-line def, single-line, one-line template, 07 single-line-def], [Value-block def, value-block, closed by a double bang, 07 multi-line-value], [Block def, block, uses the body slot, 07 block-definition], [Capture list, block, declares captures, 07 multi-capture-list], [Additive partial, block / single, merges across the file, 08 simple-additive-prefix], [Data def record, dataDef, hyphen delimiter required, 09 records], [Data def collection, dataDef, ordered list, 10 collections], [Data def scalar, dataDef, number / bool / null / prose, 09 scalar-types]]| |caption Definition forms and the AST they produce| table@

@@@pre
#lead: A one-line reusable value.

#abstract:
A multi-line value,
closed by two bangs.
!!

#callout ||label, body||
@aside(class ::label::)
...
aside@
callout#

+#authors: Ada
+#authors: Grace

#site: { name - Docs, year - 2026 }
#tags: [ ref, spec, wit ]
#count: 42
pre@@@

@aside(class note)
A single-line def @strong with strong@ a capture list renders the literal
capture list — use the block form for any def with captures. Data-def records
need the hyphen delimiter; the colon form is call-site only.

aside@

@h2 Other constructs h2@

@table |rows [[Construct, Renders as, Fixture], [Emphasis, strong / em, 02 emphasis], [Interpolation, the captured param, 07 captures-and-interpolation], [Raw-body hole, expand-time value in raw bodies, literal-nodes], [Body slot, the invocation body, 07 body-slot], [Comment, omitted from output, 03 comments], [Reference directive, pulled-in defs, 15 references], [Conditional, kept or dropped body, 12 conditionals], [Iteration, repeated body, 13 iteration], [Script, effects only — no output, 15 scripting], [Escape, the literal char, 00 lexical], [External data, a bound data def, data-loader]]| |caption Other constructs| table@

@@@pre
Wrap *bold* and _italic_ inline.

::name::

{{theme.accent}}

~ this line is a comment

reference "shared/defs.wit"

(if @author) By @author.name (end)
(if @status is shipped) Live (else) Draft (end)

(each @tags as tag) @li ::tag:: li@ (end)

<% total = lh.data.a + lh.data.b %>

\* a literal asterisk, not a mark

@load env load@
@load sales |as rows| |region West| load@
pre@@@

@aside(class note)
Emphasis marks wrap a @strong token strong@, so @@@code 3*4*5 code@@@ and
@@@code file_name_here code@@@ stay plain. Interpolation @@@code ::name:: code@@@
substitutes a @strong capture strong@ inside a def body; @@@code {{path}} code@@@
is a different hole that works @strong only strong@ inside @@@code @@ code@@@ raw
bodies.

aside@

@h2 The equivalence proof h2@

@a |href /docs/write/parameters/| One template, every call form a@: fixture
@code 26-all-param-forms/showcase.wit code@ invokes the same node thirteen ways
and asserts identical output. Form 13 (self-closing pipes) is placed
@strong last strong@ on purpose — pipes with no same-line close greedily bind to
the next close, so ordering is a real constraint, not a parser quirk.

